      "message": "The repeat check looks right to me. Would you mind moving it into a helper in `include/linux/p3s/swap.h`, so that `zram_process_walker()` keeps a one-line hook? Something like:\n\n```\nstatic inline bool p3s_swap_entry_repeats(swp_entry_t *last, swp_entry_t entry)\n{\n\tbool repeats \u003d last-\u003eval \u003d\u003d entry.val;\n\n\t*last \u003d entry;\n\treturn repeats;\n}\n```\n\nThe stub in the `#else` branch of the header\u0027s existing config block would return `false`, so builds without P3S drop the check. In the walker, before the budget check:\n\n```\n\t\tif (p3s_swap_entry_repeats(\u0026private-\u003elast_entry, entry))\n\t\t\tgoto unlock_swap_device;\n```\n\nThe comment about 4KB PTEs sharing a swap slot would then become the helper\u0027s kernel-doc.\n\nI think `have_last_entry` could go too. Swap slot 0 holds the swap header and is never allocated (`setup_swap_map()` sets `swap_map[0] \u003d SWAP_MAP_BAD`), so the zeroed `last_entry` can\u0027t match a real entry. Recording the entry before the budget check should also be fine, since nothing reads `last_entry` after the walker returns 1.",
